<body lang=EN-US style='tab-interval:.5in'>
<div class=Section1> <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span style='mso-tab-count:1'>            
</span>(1845) Order for petition of Elijah Conselor’s land<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>Cover page of the document:<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>Elijah Consellor S and Petition for Partition.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>Order for partition granted &amp; freeholders appointed by order here .... 
(names).<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>Recorded in Record Book P folio 461 &amp;c.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>Indexed.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'>To 
the Honorable the Orphans’ Court of Kent County:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>The Petition of<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'> Enoch Spruance</b> respectfully represents, That by virtue of proceedings 
in this Court returned in the year 1812 the widow’s dower in the real estate of 
a certain <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elijah Consellor</b> late of 
Little Creek Hundred in said county, who died intestate, was laid off and assigned 
to<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'> Hannah</b> widow of the said intestate, 
and the residue equally divided amongst his children agreeably to law, as will 
more fully appear by reference to the return of the said proceedings recorded 
in Book G folio 129 et seq.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>That the part so laid off and assigned to the 
said widow as her dower contains sixty six acres and thirty three perches and 
seven tenths of a perch of land more or less, and is marked on the plot recorded 
on folio 129 afsd with the letters ABBC&amp;D.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>That the said widow departed this life sometime 
in the year 1840.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>That the said intestate 
left to survive him at the time of his death five children as his heirs at law, 
viz: - <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>1st Jeremiah, 2nd Elijah, 3d Sarah, 
4th Elizabeth, 5th Benjamin.<o:p></o:p></b></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Jeremiah</b> died in the lifetime of his mother the said <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Hannah </b>intestate and left to survive him 
as his heirs at law five children viz:<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>1st 
Hester,<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>2nd Elijah,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>3d Hannah,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>4th Harriet<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>5th Jeremiah</b>;<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>that the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Hester </b>married, as her first husband, a certain <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jesse Dean who died</b>, and had by the said 
Jesse one child named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah</b>, and 
<u>after the death of the said Jesse she intermarried with and became the wife 
of a certain <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elisha Durham</b></u>, and 
afterwards in the year 1840 departed this life intestate leaving to survive her 
her said husband the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elisha Durham</b> 
and ten children besides the said<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'> Jeremiah</b>, viz. <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>1st Joel,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>2d<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>Isaac,<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>3d Elijah,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>4th 
John,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>5th Elizabeth,<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>6th David,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>7th 
Mary,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>8th Hester,<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>9th Ann,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>10th 
Clayton</b> which last has since died under age, intestate and without issue leaving 
to survive him as his heirs at law his said brothers and sisters of the whole 
blood;<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>that the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elijah 
</b>second child of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah</b> 
as aforesaid is living; that the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Hannah</b> 
third child of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah</b> is 
also living and is the <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>wife of a certain 
Perry Cork</b>;<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>that the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Harriet and Jeremiah</b> the fourth and fifth children of the said <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah both died under age</b>, intestate 
and without issue.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Elijah </b>the aforesaid second child of the intestate aforesaid <u>died 
about the year 1826</u> and after his death all and singular his interest in the 
said dower (the same being one undivided fifth part thereof) was sold at public 
vendue by the Sheriff of Kent County aforesaid and bought by your petitioner to 
whom a deed was duly made and executed by the said Sheriff.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Sarah</b> the aforesaid third child of the intestate aforesaid is living 
and is the <u>widow</u> of a certain <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Debrix Miller</b>, and is unmarried.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'> Elizabeth</b> the aforesaid fourth child of the intestate aforesaid intermarried 
with a certain <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>John Durham</b> and <u>died 
about the year 1815</u> leaving to survive her her said<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>husband and three children, viz<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>1st Ezekiel<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>2d Enoch<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>3d Mary</b>, <u>which last has since died</u> 
under age intestate and without issue.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'> Benjamin</b> the aforesaid fifth child of the intestate aforesaid in 
his lifetime <u>sold all his interest in the said dower</u> (the same being one 
undivided fifth part thereof) to the before named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Debrix Miller</b>, <u>and afterward died</u>;<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>that since then said purchaser the said <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Debrix Miller</b> has departed this life intestate 
leaving to survive him a widow the before named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Sarah</b> and six children, <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>viz<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>1st<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Josiah,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>2nd<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Elijah,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>3d<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>Rachel<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>4th<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Enoch<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>5th<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Robert<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>6th<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>Maria</b>; that the said <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Rachel</b> is the wife of a certain <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Benjamin Greenage</b>; that the said <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Maria</b> intermarried with and became the 
wife of a certain <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Benjamin Hughes</b>, 
and after the death of her father the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Debrix 
Miller</b>, <u>departed this life intestate</u> leaving to survive her her husband 
the said<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'> Benjamin Hughes</b> and two children, 
viz.<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'> John </b>and <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Rachel.<o:p></o:p></b></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the interest of the above named 
parties in the said dower is as follows:<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>that 
is to say, by dividing the same into five thousand nine hundred and forty parts, 
the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah Dean</b> is entitled 
to thirty six of those parts, and the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Joel, Isaac, Elijah, John, Elizabeth, David, Mary, Hester and Ann Durham</b> 
are each entitled to forty of those parts subject to the life estate of the said 
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elisha Durham</b> the husband of the before 
named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Hester</b> decd. who was the mother 
of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah, Joel, Isaac, Elijah, 
John, Elizabeth, David, Mary, Hester </b>and <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Ann</b> and the first child of the said <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah Consellor</b>, as tenant by the curtesy.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the before named <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elijah</b> child of the before named <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah Consellor</b> is entitled to three 
hundred and ninety six of those parts.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the before named <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Perry Cork </b>and <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Hannah</b> his wife which said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Hannah</b> 
was the third child of the before named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Jeremiah 
Consellor</b> is entitled in right of the said<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'> Hannah</b> to<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>three hundred and 
ninety six of those parts.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That your petitioner who purchased 
at Sheriff’s sale, as aforesaid, the interest of the said<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'> Elijah Consellor</b> who was the second child of the said intestate is 
entitled to one thousand one<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>hundred and 
eighty eight of those parts.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Sarah Miller</b> widow as afsd. of the before named <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Debrix Miller</b>, and third child of the 
said intestate is entitled to one thousand one<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>hundred and eighty eight of those parts.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'> Ezekiel </b>and <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Enoch Durham</b> 
children<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>as aforesaid of the before named 
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elizabeth</b> the deceased wife of the 
before named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>John Durham</b>, the said 
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elizabeth </b>being the fourth child of 
the said intestate are each entitled to five hundred and ninety four of those 
parts subject to the life estate of their father the<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>John 
Durham</b> therein, as tenant by the curtesy.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Josiah, Elijah, Enoch and Robert Miller</b>, and the said <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Benjamin Greenage </b>and <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Rachel</b> his wife in right of the said <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Rachel</b>, which said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Josiah, Elijah, Enoch,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Robert and 
Rachel</b> are children of the before named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Debrix Miller</b> decd. who was the assignee of <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Benjamin Consellor</b> who was the fifth child of the said intestate, 
are each entitled to one hundred and ninety eight of those parts subject to the 
dower therein of the <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>said Sarah Miller</b> 
widow as afsd. of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Debrix Miller</b>--and 
the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>John</b> and<b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'> Rachel Hughes</b> children as aforesaid of 
the before named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Maria</b> who was the 
wife of the before named <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Benjamin Hughes</b> 
and the sixth child of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Debrix 
Miller</b> deceased, assignee as afsd. of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Benjamin Counselor</b>, are each entitled to ninety nine of those parts<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>subject to the dower therein of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Sarah 
Miller</b> widow as afsd. of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Debrix 
Miller</b> and also to the life estate therein of their father the<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Benjamin Hughes</b> as tenant 
by the curtesy.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>That the said dower has never been 
divided.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Your petitioner therefore prays 
the Court to appoint freeholders to divide the same according to law &amp;c.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span style='mso-tab-count:6'>                                                                       
</span>And he will ever &amp;c--<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span style='mso-tab-count:6'>                                                                        
</span>Enoch Spruance<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>Know all men by these Presents, That 
We have nominated and by these presents do nominate and appoint <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Joseph P. Comegys</b> Attorney at law of the 
town of Dover Kent County and State of Delaware, our true and lawful attorney 
for us and in our place and stead to enter satisfaction of our and each of our 
shares in a certain recognizance entered into in the Orphans’ Court of Kent County 
aforesaid at the September Term <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>1845 </b>by 
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Presley Spruance </b>and <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Enoch Spruance </b>of the town of Smyrna in 
Kent County aforesaid upon the acceptance by them of that part of the real estate 
of <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elijah Consellor</b> deceased which 
in the division of the said estate was laid off to his widow<b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'> Hannah Consellor</b>, and which at the said 
September Term 1845 (the said Hannah being dead) was valued by the freeholders 
appointed by the said the Orphans’ Court on the division of the same, and was 
accepted by the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Presley Spruance </b>and 
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Enoch Spruance</b> as parties entitled 
by assignment of the interest of one of the heirs at law of the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Elijah 
Consellor</b>, hereby ratifying and confirming all our said attorney may lawfully 
do in the premises--we hereby acknowledge that we have respectively secured from 
the said <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Presley Spruance </b>and <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Enoch Spruance</b> full satisfaction of our 
respective shares of the said recognizance.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'><span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                        </span>Witness our hands &amp; 
seals respectively this<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>(<i
style='mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>blank</i>)<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>day of AD 184(<i style='mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>blank</i>).<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'>Signed, 
sealed &amp; delivered<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>              </span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'>in 
presence of <span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                           </span>Benjamin 
Greenage<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Seal<span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>           </span><u>Marks made by</u>:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:Arial'>D. 
